    {
     "_comment": "the log opens from the bar, on any page, without a request",
     "selector": "#jobbar-toggle",
     "contains": "view log"
    }
   ],
   "_disabled_comment": [
    "These three are enabled by the dashboard's own fixtures and locked only",
    "by the bar: this is the bar's doing, not the page's. The restore path is",
    "asserted by mutation \"job bar never unlocks the controls again\" \u2014 a",
    "static spec cannot see a lock that was never released, so it has to be",
    "broken in the template to know it is tested."
   ],
   "expectDisabled": [
    "#upd-btn"
   ],
   "_body_comment": [
    "data-jobbusy is the machine-wide lock and must still be set after every",
    "control has been driven: a panel re-rendering its own buttons can clear",
    "`disabled`, and only a re-asserted end-state catches a bar that forgot."
   ],
   "_busy_scope": [
    "Checked at load and again after the whole sweep. In between, driving a",
    "select case runs the dashboard's own panel renderer, which repaints its",
    "buttons and owns this attribute until the bar's next poll."
   ],
   "expectBodyAttr": {
    "data-jobbusy": "1"
   }
